    "title": "Dayton road closed after crash in intersection - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Southall ,\n2 hours ago\nDAYTON, Ohio ( WDTN ) – The Montgomery County Sheriff’s Office is currently investigating a crash that occurred at approximately 1:15 p.m. on Wednesday, Oct. 1.\nDeputies from the Montgomery County Sheriff’s Office were dispatched to the intersection of Turner Road and Philadelphia Drive following reports of a multiple-vehicle crash. One vehicle was reportedly on fire and entrapped.\nUpon arrival, the deputies found that a vehicle had run the red light westbound on Turner Road and had struck two vehicles traveling southbound on Philadelphia Drive in the intersection.\nKettering woman dies after crash in Clinton Co. The suspect was ejected from the vehicle and later taken to the hospital with non-life-threatening injuries.\nTwo people were rescued from the vehicles that had been struck. The victims were taken to local hospitals with non-life-threatening injuries.\nTurner Road was closed for approximately two hours and 45 minutes following the incident.\nThe crash remains under investigation by the Traffic Services Unit of the Montgomery County Sheriff’s Office.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.\n1",
